WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.509 --> 00:00:02.447
- [Voiceover] It's red and pricey.

00:00:02.447 --> 00:00:04.952
It's a critter and a delicacy.

00:00:04.952 --> 00:00:07.292
It's the crème de la crème of seafood,

00:00:07.292 --> 00:00:10.195
but this beloved summertime
favorite was once thought of

00:00:10.195 --> 00:00:12.552
as the poor man's food.

00:00:12.552 --> 00:00:13.385
Say what?

00:00:15.608 --> 00:00:17.712
It is said that in the early 16th century

00:00:17.712 --> 00:00:19.709
as the first Pilgrims began to settle

00:00:19.709 --> 00:00:21.327
in bay areas of America

00:00:21.327 --> 00:00:23.962
that the oceans overfloweth with lobster.

00:00:23.962 --> 00:00:25.699
No, literally, they overfloweth.

00:00:25.699 --> 00:00:29.022
Imagine a shore with a
lobster wall two feet tall.

00:00:29.022 --> 00:00:31.248
As one would expect,
the settlers ate them up

00:00:31.248 --> 00:00:33.763
until, like anything
eaten three times a day,

00:00:33.763 --> 00:00:34.865
they got sick of them,

00:00:34.865 --> 00:00:38.288
eventually deeming them
the cockroaches of the sea.

00:00:38.288 --> 00:00:40.710
After that, lobsters
were used as fertilizer,

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:43.803
fish bait, and ultimately prison food.

00:00:43.803 --> 00:00:46.063
They were fed so often to inmates

00:00:46.063 --> 00:00:48.916
that there was even a law
enacted to protect said inmates

00:00:48.916 --> 00:00:51.935
from cruel and unusual lobster punishment.

00:00:51.935 --> 00:00:54.555
So, then how did lobster
become the succulent delicacy

00:00:54.555 --> 00:00:55.888
we all know and love?

00:00:55.888 --> 00:00:57.626
Fast forward to the mid 1800s.

00:00:57.626 --> 00:01:00.186
Canned food became a
thing, as did the railroad.

00:01:00.186 --> 00:01:03.182
Lobsters were canned and
shipped to Middle America.

00:01:03.182 --> 00:01:05.584
At the same time, Middle
Americans started traveling

00:01:05.584 --> 00:01:07.591
to New England for fresh lobster.

00:01:07.591 --> 00:01:10.476
By the late 1880s, prices began to surge.

00:01:10.476 --> 00:01:13.580
And by World War II, lobsters
become the pricey speciality

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:15.596
we've all grown to enjoy.

00:01:15.596 --> 00:01:18.679
(jaunty piano music)

